                    <span class="badge platform">Arcade</span>
                    <span class="badge coming-soon" title="Queued in Qwen3.5-3D-Coder synthesis pipeline">⏳ Coming Soon</span>
                </div>
                <span class="world-id">#823</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3>Pac-Man</h3>
                <h4>Symmetrical Blue Vector Wall Dot Labyrinths</h4>
                <img class="world-img" src="https://cdn.wikimg.net/en/strategywiki/images/a/ab/Google_pac_man.jpg" alt="Pac-Man - Symmetrical Blue Vector Wall Dot Labyrinths reference image" loading="lazy">
                <div class="description-container">
                    <p class="description collapsed" id="desc-823">Symmetrical Blue Vector Wall Dot Labyrinths, Pac-Man (Arcade). Atari snapped up the rights to bring the arcade hit home, and let down millions of fans with a sub-par conversion on what was their most popular home system at the time, the Atari 2600. Despite Pac-Man's popularity, no official explanation has ever been provided by Namco as to why Pac-Man has to run around a maze, gobble the pellets, and avoid the ghosts. This is the first game in thePac-Manseries.</p>
                    <button class="expand-btn" onclick="toggleDesc('823', this)">Read more ▾</button>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card-footer">
                <span class="play-btn disabled-btn">⏳ Coming Soon — Queued</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="world-card card-coming-soon" data-status="coming-soon">
            <div class="card-header">
                <div>
                    <span class="badge platform">Arcade</span>
                    <span class="badge coming-soon" title="Queued in Qwen3.5-3D-Coder synthesis pipeline">⏳ Coming Soon</span>
                </div>
                <span class="world-id">#824</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3>Ms. Pac-Man</h3>
                <h4>Pastel Pink, Blue & Orange Multi-Exit Maze Layouts</h4>
                
                <div class="description-container">
                    <p class="description collapsed" id="desc-824">Pastel Pink, Blue & Orange Multi-Exit Maze Layouts, Ms. Pac-Man (Arcade). WhenPac-Manwas still hot in the arcades, a small company known as GCC, or General Computer Corp., was in the business of making arcade "enhancements" which were essentially small hacks designed to make certain games more appealing. GCC was known for an add on that they had sold forAtari'sMissile Commandwhen they sat down to design a hack for Pac-Man. Pac-Man in an effort to entice more females to play arcade games.</p>
                    <button class="expand-btn" onclick="toggleDesc('824', this)">Read more ▾</button>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card-footer">
                <span class="play-btn disabled-btn">⏳ Coming Soon — Queued</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        
