                <div>
                    <span class="badge platform">Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800</span>
                    <span class="badge coming-soon" title="Queued in Qwen3.5-3D-Coder synthesis pipeline">⏳ Coming Soon</span>
                </div>
                <span class="world-id">#871</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3>Sinistar</h3>
                <h4>Mining Asteroid Belts & Derelict Mechanical Void</h4>
                
                <div class="description-container">
                    <p class="description collapsed" id="desc-871">Mining Asteroid Belts & Derelict Mechanical Void, Sinistar (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). Due to Sinistars arrival close to the video game market crash of1983, and perhaps due to its complexity, Sinistar saw no official conversions to home platforms until it began showing up in classic compilation titles in the mid 90s. Sinistaris an arcade game released byWilliamsin1982. At first glance, it appears to be an amalgamation of a few existing arcade games such asAsteroidsandDefender.</p>
                    <button class="expand-btn" onclick="toggleDesc('871', this)">Read more ▾</button>
                </div>
            </div>
