                <div>
                    <span class="badge platform">Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800</span>
                    <span class="badge coming-soon" title="Queued in Qwen3.5-3D-Coder synthesis pipeline">⏳ Coming Soon</span>
                </div>
                <span class="world-id">#873</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3>Marble Madness</h3>
                <h4>Sloping Pastel Concrete Courses, Funnels & Drop-offs</h4>
                
                <div class="description-container">
                    <p class="description collapsed" id="desc-873">Sloping Pastel Concrete Courses, Funnels & Drop-offs, Marble Madness (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). Beginning in1986, the game was ported to numerous platforms with different companies handling the conversions; several home versions were published byElectronic Arts, Tiger Electronics released handheld and tabletop LCD versions of the game, and it was ported to theNintendo Entertainment SystembyRare. Marble Madnessis anarcadevideo game designed by Mark Cerny, and published byAtari Gamesin1984.</p>
                    <button class="expand-btn" onclick="toggleDesc('873', this)">Read more ▾</button>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card-footer">
                <span class="play-btn disabled-btn">⏳ Coming Soon — Queued</span>
