            <div class="card-header">
                <div>
                    <span class="badge platform">Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800</span>
                    <span class="badge coming-soon" title="Queued in Qwen3.5-3D-Coder synthesis pipeline">⏳ Coming Soon</span>
                </div>
                <span class="world-id">#874</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3>Tempest</h3>
                <h4>3D Geometric Vector Tubes, Web Chasms & Spikes</h4>
                
                <div class="description-container">
                    <p class="description collapsed" id="desc-874">3D Geometric Vector Tubes, Web Chasms & Spikes, Tempest (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). However, unlike Asteroids, it was difficult to take the crisp clean graphics that defined Tempest and port them successfully to early home consoles. While prototypes have been discovered for theAtari 2600and theAtari 5200, official conversions were not released until 1987, when the game appeared on several popular British home computers. This is the first game in theTempestseries.</p>
                    <button class="expand-btn" onclick="toggleDesc('874', this)">Read more ▾</button>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card-footer">
                <span class="play-btn disabled-btn">⏳ Coming Soon — Queued</span>
