                <div>
                    <span class="badge platform">Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800</span>
                    <span class="badge coming-soon" title="Queued in Qwen3.5-3D-Coder synthesis pipeline">⏳ Coming Soon</span>
                </div>
                <span class="world-id">#878</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3>Quantum</h3>
                <h4>Atomic Nucleus Energy Fields & Subatomic Particles</h4>
                
                <div class="description-container">
                    <p class="description collapsed" id="desc-878">Atomic Nucleus Energy Fields & Subatomic Particles, Quantum (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). This game did not fare very well in the arcades (and only around 500 cabinets were ever produced); many of the unsold (and returned) ones were sold to either the general public or employees of Atari. The Nucleuses shall also join together to form bonds (which can again kill the probe when they are red) - and white particles move vertically, while those of other colours move diagonally.</p>
                    <button class="expand-btn" onclick="toggleDesc('878', this)">Read more ▾</button>
                </div>
