                <div>
                    <span class="badge platform">Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800</span>
                    <span class="badge coming-soon" title="Queued in Qwen3.5-3D-Coder synthesis pipeline">⏳ Coming Soon</span>
                </div>
                <span class="world-id">#879</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3>Space Duel</h3>
                <h4>Multi-Colored Vector Geometry Voids & Cosmic Minefields</h4>
                <img class="world-img" src="https://cdn.wikimg.net/en/strategywiki/images/1/1b/Space_Duel_Select.png" alt="Space Duel - Multi-Colored Vector Geometry Voids & Cosmic Minefields reference image" loading="lazy">
                <div class="description-container">
                    <p class="description collapsed" id="desc-879">Multi-Colored Vector Geometry Voids & Cosmic Minefields, Space Duel (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). Partly for the same reason that Tempest was never converted until gaming systems had much better resolution, and partly because many of the features it presented, like shields and cooperative play were already features in some of the home conversions of Asteroids. Each ship contains a limited amount of Shield power as well. Space Duelis an arcade game released in1980byAtari.</p>
                    <button class="expand-btn" onclick="toggleDesc('879', this)">Read more ▾</button>
                </div>
            </div>
